# Root build context (api image: docker-compose service "api", context ".")
# Goal: keep secrets, ops backups, history and dev-only payloads out of images (audit S6).
# NOTE: wff-builder/keystore/test.keystore is the PUBLIC dev certificate — it stays in the
# dev image because the builder needs a keystore. Production signing must use WFF_KEYSTORE
# (see wff-builder/wff_builder.py signing mode).

# --- secrets & ops payloads (never into any image layer) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.tools-backup-*
credentials/
*.pem
*.key
!wff-builder/keystore/test.keystore
*.jks
*.keystore
!wff-builder/keystore/test.keystore

# --- git & CI metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
.github/

# --- logs & caches ---
*.log
logs/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.audit-venv/
.venv/
node_modules/
*.md
!README.md

# --- runtime outputs (rebuild artifacts never belong in image) ---
tmp/
*.apk

# --- dev-only payloads: built separately or not needed by the API ---
web/
docs/
experiments/
tests/
skills/
scripts/
projects/
